# Product glossary

When writing or editing **user-facing product copy** (app UI, FAQs, empty states, settings descriptions, help text, README product descriptions), follow [`docs/glossary.md`](docs/glossary.md).

## Hard rule

Never describe the in-product agent as **"the AI"**, **"the bot"**, **"the assistant"**, or **"Lumantic AI"**. Say **Lumantic**.

Examples:
- "New things Lumantic picked up…"
- "Ask Lumantic anything"
- "Learned by Lumantic"
- "Let Lumantic query this source…"

Marketing category language (for example "AI-native" on the landing page) is fine. Generated Cloudflare type comments and similar third-party docs are out of scope.

When you introduce a new user-facing concept, add it to `docs/glossary.md` in the same change.
